<title>PERU: Peru's January wheat output falls to 50 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Peru's January wheat output falls to 50 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's January wheat production fell to 50 tonnes from 1,602 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Wheat imports in January rose 1.0 percent to $16.26 million, compared with the same month last year, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Peru's wheat is grown mostly in the central and southeastern Andean regions.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
</text>
